@page "/products/services"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Serga Services"; ViewData["Description"] = "Turn services into self-service with a customer-facing catalog, requests and provider context."; }
<section class="hero container detail-hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Serga Services</p><h1>Turn services<br /><em>into self-service.</em></h1><p class="hero-description">One place to discover, order and manage services. A clear route from each request to the people or systems that fulfil it.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/platform">Explore the platform <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><partial name="_ServicesMockup" /></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The customer-facing service layer</p><h2>A simpler way<br />to get things <em>done.</em></h2><p>When services live across emails, portals and individual contacts, knowing where to start becomes work in itself.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>Discover what’s available</h3><p>Bring Wi-Fi, access, parking, meeting rooms, cleaning and catering into a service catalog shaped around the customer, user and location.</p></article><article><h3>Request with context</h3><p>Connect each order to the right organization and location, with approvals where required and a clear view of progress.</p></article><article><h3>Connect the right provider</h3><p>Route requests to an internal team, an external provider, a business system or an API-enabled technical system.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="detail-section container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">From discovery to fulfilment</p><h2>One request.<br /><em>A clear path.</em></h2><p>A tenant requests visitor access. Serga brings the request and location together, then routes it to the responsible provider. Technical delivery depends on the provider and available integrations.</p></div><ol class="workflow"><li><span class="eyebrow">01</span><strong>Customer / User</strong><p>See the services available to you.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">02</span><strong>Discover service</strong><p>Choose a service and understand the options.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">03</span><strong>Request / Order</strong><p>Supply the information needed to fulfil it.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">04</span><strong>Approval if required</strong><p>Bring the right decision-maker into the request.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">05</span><strong>Provider / System</strong><p>Connect the request to the delivery team or underlying system.</p></li><li><span class="eyebrow">06</span><strong>Fulfilment</strong><p>Keep the customer informed as the service is delivered.</p></li></ol></section>

<section class="context-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Independently useful. Better together.</p><h2>The service relationship.<br /><em>In its own right.</em></h2><p>Traditional operational systems manage the building or infrastructure. Serga Services focuses on the customer-facing service relationship.</p></div><div class="capability-grid"><article><h3>Useful on its own</h3><p>Start with a catalog, requests and provider context. Revenue, Contracts and Leasing are optional.</p></article><article><h3>Alongside existing systems</h3><p>Keep specialist operations in their existing systems. Automatic provisioning depends on the service and integration; it is not universal.</p></article><article><h3>Connected when useful</h3><p>An Internet service order can connect to recurring commercial terms in Revenue, or to a related agreement in Contracts.</p></article></div></div></section>

<section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Make the connection</p><h2>Make services easier<br /><em>to access.</em></h2><a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Book a demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span class="cta-tagline">Your gateway to services</span></div></section>
